# The Learjet 35A's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/learjet35a.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 60% and 86% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the elevators from 0.4 m out to 2.2 m, hinged three tenths of the
# chord forward of the trailing edge;
# the rudder from 3.0 m above the origin to 4.3 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing 3.25..5.14 at 3.60 m, 3.17..4.82 at 5.16 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  3.724 -3.602 -1.956  3.581 -5.163 -2.007  0.000 0.563 0.168
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  3.724 3.602 -1.956  3.581 5.163 -2.007  0.000 0.563 0.168
# tail -2.31..-0.91 at 0.40 m, -2.62..-2.00 at 2.20 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -1.891 -0.400 -4.484  -2.434 -2.200 -4.486  0.000 0.504 0.160
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -1.891 0.400 -4.484  -2.434 2.200 -4.486  0.000 0.504 0.160
# fin -1.70..0.48 at -3.00 m, -1.98..-0.07 at -4.30 m
surface rudder          fcs/rudder-pos-rad         left  -1.046 0.000 -3.000  -1.409 0.000 -4.300  0.000 0.771 0.289
